  "status_text": "A quiet stretch on the checker: two more seven-vertex graphs where a single NOT gate saves nothing, and one more value step pinning a four-input function at exactly 6 gates, all from outside proofs. Now on the banner: no circuit of at most 11 AND, OR and NOT gates multiplies two 2-by-2 Boolean matrices. Still open where the tables did not close: the Heawood graph with NOT gates allowed, between 20 and 27 gates. Small cases are a table, not a law.",
